# Direct backend dependencies — the human-maintained source of intent.
#
# This file is NOT installed directly. It is compiled into the fully-pinned,
# cross-platform lock `requirements.txt` (every direct AND transitive package
# at an exact version) via:
#
#   python -m uv pip compile --universal requirements.in \
#       -c <(pip freeze) -o requirements.txt
#
# CI installs the compiled requirements.txt, so builds are reproducible and can
# never silently drift onto an untested dependency version. To bump a dep: edit
# the constraint here, re-compile, and rebuild-test the desktop app before
# releasing — never let CI float versions. See desktop/finzytrack.spec.

